<article class="env-lemma" id="01NC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01NC">Lemma <span data-tag="01NC">27.12.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a graded ring. Let $X = \text{Proj}(S)$. The functor $F$ defined above is representable by the scheme $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have seen above that the functor $F_ d$ corresponds to the open subscheme $U_ d \subset X$. Moreover the transformation of functors $F_ d \to F_{d'}$ (if $d | d'$) defined above corresponds to the inclusion morphism $U_ d \to U_{d'}$ (see discussion above). Hence to show that $F$ is represented by $X$ it suffices to show that $T \to X$ for a quasi-compact scheme $T$ ends up in some $U_ d$, and that for a general scheme $T$ we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (T, X) = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{V \subset T\text{ quasi-compact open}} \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (V, X).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       These verifications are omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>